zune-capi: fix double free in zil_status_free

`ZStatus` owns its `message` buffer and `impl Drop for ZStatus` frees it, so
freeing `message` manually before `status.drop_in_place()` frees the same
pointer twice and every `zil_status_free` call aborts the process.  Dropping
the status is enough: `zil_status_new` always installs a live allocation in
`message`, and the `*status = ZStatus::new(..)` error assignments elsewhere
replace an already initialised status, so each message is freed exactly once.

--- a/crates/zune-capi/src/errno.rs
+++ b/crates/zune-capi/src/errno.rs
@@ -160,7 +160,6 @@
 #[no_mangle]
 pub extern "C" fn zil_status_free(status: *mut ZStatus) {
     if !status.is_null() {
-        unsafe { zil_free((*status).message.cast()) }
         // free object
         unsafe { status.drop_in_place() }
 
